hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan where I  answer your questions today I'm going to  be talking about what courses you should  take in university or in school to help  you prepare to be an entrepreneur so  today's question comes from Martha we  wrote in asking Evan I'm consuming a  bachelor's degree in procurement Supply  Management heading to my second year in  August as an entrepreneur can you please  advise me on another course I can do  alongside dine order to be skilled so  thank you for the question Martha a  great question one that I get a lot from  young entrepreneurs who are in school or  starting school because they want to  start their own business and hoping to  use their education to help them as much  as possible from my own experience is  kind of all I can share with you i watch  the University of Toronto and  unfortunately there weren't too many  courses that would help me with my  entrepreneurship skills there was one  course in small business management so  if there is anything that that is about  entrepreneurship or small business you  definitely want to take that on what  else I would look at is try to find  something related to marketing finance  accounting those might give you some of  the hard skills that you need to run  your business but what I would do is try  to connect with some of the clubs that  happen at the university I think that  the the greatest experience that I got  out of the university was being able to  find people who also were interested in  entrepreneurship and we actually started  our own first business out of university  so I was running my company while taking  classes in university so trying to find  like-minded people see if there's an  entrepreneur Club or small business club  that you can join up with or if there's  any seminars or events because these  people you know they're they'll give you  some ideas and advice but also could  become lifelong friends and business  partners as you continue to to grow up  you know and as these people graduate  and start their own businesses you have  people you can potentially connect to  and rely on down the line so I try to  think beyond just the courses and also  try to connect with the community of  entrepreneurs around you if your  eventual goal is to start your own  business I'd also look at potentially  starting up  partnering with an existing company and  taking on a part-time job so find a  company who is doing exactly what you  want to do smaller companies somebody  who's either a solo entrepreneur or has  a few employees but not not a big  company and try to learn as much as you  can about their business how they got  started all the operations you know  entrepreneurs always need help so if you  can prove to be a valuable resource for  them  then that can start giving you some  ideas and how they run their business  and give you some thoughts as well as if  this is the type of business you want to  run or not a lot of times we have ideas  for businesses but once we get into it  that is a terrible idea  so being paid by somebody to learn is a  great opportunity to in a low-risk way  learn about the industry find out if  it's for you gain some skills and that  can be in addition to doing your regular  university coursework one final  suggestion is helping that really helped  me with my university career is I was  starting my business while I was at  university I was in third year I believe  and what I actually did was I talked to  one of my marketing professors and  created my own course with him so I  don't know if this is an option at your  University or not but we were able to do  it at University of Toronto where I  created my own course and with with this  professor he basically gave me a credit  so we didn't have an exam what we had to  kind of come together and figure out how  we get how I was gonna you know what the  course is gonna be about housings in my  research what findings I was gonna  create and I basically made the course  about my business and I was able to run  my business get his advice and also get  a credit for it so you have to talk to  you know professors they have to know  your they have to be willing to mentor  you for the semester people to give you  that credit but it's another opportunity  to potentially use your university or  school education to be able to get you  know more out of it to help you build  your business so one look for any  entrepreneur small business courses if  they don't exist look for anything that  might give you some hard skills  marketing finance accounting any of  those kind of courses to trying to get  involved again in the university  community look at clubs that you might  be able to join or any events or  seminars that are happening and through  see if you might be able to create your  own course with a professor  around the topic that is interesting  that can help you launch your business  and then for also again look to see if  you might be able to get a part-time job  outside of the University where you can  learn from an entrepreneur and also gain  the skills that you need when you are  ready to launch your own business so  hopefully that helped Martha a great  question I love answering that and love  helping young entrepreneurs for those of  you watching if you like the video  please give it a thumbs up below what  makes you want to do more of these  videos for you guys and if you have any  advice to Martha or you have a question  of your own feel free to leave in the  comments below I always read the  comments and I love reading the comments  that it always makes my day so please  leave a comment if you can  and we'll see you on the next episode  you
 

